from pathlib import Path
import json,hashlib
P=Path(__file__).resolve().parent
rows=[
('In later-game setup with five players, how much favor goes in each bank, what is on the banners, and what resources and warbands start on each kind of player board?', 'Four favor per suit bank (three with two–four players). People’s Favor normal with one favor, Darkest Secret one secret. Chancellor two favor,one secret,three purple board warbands; other players one favor,one secret,three board warbands (own color Exile,purple Citizen). All full Supply.', 'Law 1.4–15','Later-game resource setup and player-count branch'),
('How is the Chronicled map dealt, where are starting Imperial garrisons placed, and which sites receive favor/secrets during later-game setup?', 'Deal saved sites/attached cards Cradle then Provinces then Hinterland top-down. Two purple at topmost faceup Cradle, one at each other faceup site with denizen or intact edifice; ruin alone insufficient. Put printed favor/secrets on prompted sites from bank; Chancellor allocates insufficient favor.', 'Law 1.1,1.12,1.16','Saved-map and intact-versus-ruined garrison setup'),
('May later-game players choose a Citizen board or any pawn location? Does starting Citizen receive a relic, and who starts with a banner/title?', 'Non-Chancellors choose in turn order among boards on saved sides, so Citizen only if saved Citizen. No starting relic for Citizen. Pawns any faceup site except Chancellor top Cradle. Chancellor Oathkeeper, gets Darkest Secret for Devotion or People’s Favor for People.', 'Law 1.7–15,1.23; Playbook p30','Inherited status versus in-play grant'),
('Describe later-game discard seeding, starting adviser selection and Vision counting. Are starting Reliquary relic placements chosen or random?', 'Seed each discard with one of three total bottom-world-deck cards; each player draws three bottom cards, then turn order chooses facedown adviser and discards other two using pawn region after placing pawn. Advance Visions Drawn for drawn Visions. Four Reliquary relics randomly one per space.', 'Law 1.17–23; Errata 1.17','Bottom draws and random Reliquary setup'),
('In first-game packet setup, which sites/pawns/garrisons/denizens/advisers are faceup or facedown, and where is Ivory Eye?', 'Plains top Cradle,purple pawn,two purple garrison,Longbows; Mountain top Provinces,Red/Blue pawns,one purple,Taming Charm; Rocky Coast top Hinterland,Yellow pawn,one purple,Elders. Other sites facedown. Facedown advisers Chancellor Forest Paths,Red Animal Playmates,Blue Naysayers,Yellow A Small Favor. Ivory Eye facedown at Mountain. Preserve packet deck order.', 'Playbook pp6–7','First-game tutorial configuration distinct from later setup'),
('Can you act at a remote ruled site to Muster/Trade, use a normal Action power there, or use a battle plan at your pawn site that you do not rule? How do persistent powers differ?', 'Muster/Trade only pawn site. Normal card power accessible by ruling card or pawn at its site, so remote ruled Action accessible. Battle plan requires rule, pawn alone insufficient. Persistent black-thick-braid power affects specified players ignoring ordinary access.', 'Law 5.2–3,7.1.1,7.1.4,7.5.1','Power access versus site action and persistent exception'),
('A defensive battle plan costs favor and a secret. Where do those go when used outside your turn, when is the secret ready again, and can that plan already hold resources?', 'Favor immediately matching bank,secret stays own board facedown,cannot place/burn facedown to pay; ready at own Rest. Battle-plan payment allowed on occupied card once per Campaign. Does not allow Muster/Trade on occupied card.', 'Law 7.1.2,7.5.3,4.3.2','Out-of-turn resource exhaustion exception'),
('When are ordinary action modifiers used, may the same modifier apply twice to one action or to later actions, and may an active modifier be discarded?', 'At modified action start,in any order; each once per action, only current action. No-cost modifier can modify multiple different actions. Usually optional except must/cannot; cannot discard while modifying current action.', 'Law 7.4','Modifier activation lifetime and protected discard'),
('What is the timing order for When Played powers, how often may Wake/Rest powers happen, and may a paid power be used if it will have no effect?', 'When Played mandatory after playing faceup,after site-favor gain,Homeland effects and modifiers. Wake once each in Wake; Rest optional once each at end Rest. May pay/use even zero effect,resolve as much as possible except may parts.', 'Law 7.1.3,7.3; Errata 7.1.3','Standalone power timing and no-effect payment'),
('What do tree, person and chain restrictions do to faceup play/move/swap/discard, and how are two adviser-limit reductions combined and checked when played?', 'Tree site-only,person adviser-only,also move/swap; locked cannot discard/move/swap once played except Chronicle. Facedown banners inactive. Use lowest changed adviser limit,not additive; discard to satisfy new limit before playing card,not old limit. Locked cards remain protected.', 'Law 7.2,7.6.4; Errata 7.6.4','Restrictions and prospective new-limit check'),
('Who can play Conspiracy, what exact theft conditions/cost apply, can two advisers match one enemy adviser, and where does Conspiracy end?', 'Anyone even Imperials. Burn one secret,take one relic/banner from player whose pawn at own site; two own faceup advisers each match suit of any enemy adviser,can both match same adviser. Does not replace revealed true Vision; banner seizure applies; Conspiracy goes box even no theft.', 'Law 5.1.4.IV; Reference p1','False Vision theft and final destination'),
('May you freely discard a faceup adviser, move warbands onto an empty site, or pick up the last site warband? What changes with Citizens and co-located Imperial pawns?', 'No voluntary faceup discard unless rule prompts; no ordinary drop on empty bandit site; pick up all but last own site warband. Drop only at ruled pawn site. Citizen pickup requires Chancellor permission. Imperial pawns co-located can give/take board warbands with other player permission. Bandit Crown permits last physical pickup.', 'Law 6.5,5.1.4.II,7.6.5; Playbook p32','Warband movement restrictions/Imperial transfer'),
('What relics can you peek at without paying Supply, and may a relic peeked at earlier be inspected again after moving away?', 'Any facedown relic at own pawn site; any previously peeked specific relic again from any site. Scepter holder can peek Reliquary (subject cannot use Scepter taken this turn). Other sites’ unpeeked relics require power.', 'Law 6.3–4; Grand Scepter','Remote memory-peek exception'),
('If the Scepter holder exiles a Citizen, how is favor payment calculated, which warbands change color, and does this end the recipient’s Act?', 'Pay five,+one for Citizen Oathkeeper,+one Citizen People’s Favor,minus one payer Oathkeeper,minus one payer People’s Favor. Flip Exile,replace board purple with own color,refresh full; map garrisons stay purple. Does not by itself end recipient Act.', 'Law 6.7','Forced exile cost modifiers and retained garrisons'),
('How is self-exile paid, who is prohibited from doing it, what warbands change, and does Act continue?', 'Citizen gives Scepter holder favor equal board warbands plus secrets on own board and denizen/relic/edifice cards. Scepter holder cannot self-exile. Flip Exile,replace board purple with own color,full Supply,end Act. Map purple stays.', 'Law 6.8','Self-exile distinct payment/status/turn ending'),
('Two players tie the current title holder; later the holder falls behind two tied leaders. Who holds title, and when is Supremacy transferred during Campaign?', 'Current holder keeps when tied for goal. If holder no longer meets goal,chooses among tied qualifying others. New recipient Oathkeeper-side. Supremacy transfer after Campaign ends,not temporary mid-Campaign losses. Empire collective purple rule credits Chancellor.', 'Law 2.11; Errata 2.11','Incumbent tie privilege and end-action reassessment'),
('An attack-die pool is empty and a battle plan removes an attack die. What happens? Which battle plans do bandits use and in what sequence do sides choose plans?', 'For each removal from empty attack pool,add defense die. Attacker chooses ruled plans once each then defender; bandits use all ruled plans with no cost. Plan resources do not block paying its plan cost.', 'Law 5.5.3,7.5','Empty pool conversion and automated neutral defense'),
('After skulls leave an attacking force of five warbands, the attacker loses. How many die and where do survivors go? Does winning defender take attacker’s relics?', 'Kill half remaining force rounded down:two,leaving three on attacker board. Only victorious attacker resolves declared targets; winning defender takes no attacker relics. Skulls already removed before halving.', 'Law 5.5.5–7','Defeated-attacker branch and loss timing'),
('A defender’s pawn is away from attacker and every targeted site. Do board warbands defend, and do warbands at untargeted sites defend? How are shield doubles applied?', 'No board force unless pawn at attacker/targeted site; only targeted-site garrisons add,not untargeted sites. Doubles multiply rolled shields exponentially,not warband defense. No intrinsic warband defense dice.', 'Law 5.5.4; Playbook p32','Conditional mobile-force defense and shield multiplier domain'),
('Are warbands, favor, secrets and dice component-limited? If a requested gain exceeds a source, what is done, and can you intentionally burn extra resources?', 'Warbands/favor/cards limited; secrets/dice unlimited. Gain/take maximum possible from source,not more; boards/banks no cap unless specified. Cannot place/burn/sacrifice beyond prompted cost/requirement.', 'Law 9.3,9.5','Component-shortfall and no-unprompted-loss rules'),
('Which game information is private and public? May a holder show a facedown adviser or lie about its identity?', 'Private facedown fronts,discard fronts,world-deck count and backs beyond top. Public all else including discard counts/backs and board favor,secrets,warbands. Holder may peek/show facedown adviser and players may lie about private info; cannot mix advisers indistinguishably.', 'Law 9.4','Private information boundaries'),
('How do must, cannot, ignore and must-if-able interact; which book takes priority; do a Give restriction and a Take restriction mean the same thing?', 'Cannot beats must,which beats ordinary; ignore overrides specifically named must/cannot. Must-if-able fulfilled when possible,otherwise no penalty. Law beats Playbook/aids except Site Reference,nonitalic beats reminder. Give/Take distinct; restricting one does not change other.', 'Law 9.1–2; Errata Glossary','Rules hierarchy and distinct transfer verbs'),
('Are ordinary promises or free resource gifts binding/legal? What exceptions exist, including Reliquary relics and Tribunal?', 'Ordinary promises nonbinding; unprompted resource transfer not authorized. Citizenship and powers saying binding bind agreed listed things if able. Only Citizenship offer can exchange Reliquary relic; Tribunal binding favor/secrets and future actions,disputed breach coin flip.', 'Law 6.6.1,7.6.3,9.6; Reference p2','Negotiation permissions and binding exceptions'),
('What happens when each of the four Reliquary spaces is uncovered for Chancellor: Brutal, Decadent, Careless and Greedy?', 'Brutal: when Chancellor attacker,defeated player even self kills all force. Decadent: travel Provinces/Hinterland→Cradle no Supply; to Hinterland +1 Supply. Careless: Trade gains one extra favor even secret trade; secret trade gains one fewer secret. Greedy: draw two extra on Search,still stops at world Vision,cannot Search if cost >2 Supply. Mandatory uncovered modifiers.', 'Law setup illustration; Playbook p3 Reliquary','Four revealed mandatory modifier branches'),
('Which winner can build or repair an edifice in Chronicle, how many, where, and may a new edifice replace a denizen at a site already holding a ruin?', 'Only Chancellor/Citizen winner,one build or repair. Build at ruled site with no edifice intact or ruined,replace matching denizen by intact Archive edifice,denizen to world deck. Or repair ruled ruin by flipping intact. No building over an existing ruin.', 'Law 8.3.1; Playbook Chronicle aid p4','Imperial-only edifice construction and occupancy'),
('In Chronicle, which sites are discarded, where do their attached cards go, and what happens to retained sites with intact edifices not ruled by winner?', 'Discard sites unless winner rules or intact edifice exists;shuffle sites into deck,denizens to discard,relics to relic deck,ruined edifices Archive. At retained non-winner sites flip intact edifice to ruin and discard denizens there. Set aside all ruin sites with attached ruin,denizens,relics in map order; remove all pawns/resources/warbands from map.', 'Law 8.3.2–4; Errata 8.3.3','Preservation and ruin attachment branch'),
('Give the ordered Chronicle process for filling empty map slots, including the reverse ordering of ruins and faceup-site guarantee.', 'Non-ruins: fill Cradle top-down with Cradle then Provinces then Hinterland top-down; Provinces top-down push then import Hinterland; push Hinterland up. Ruins saved in top-to-bottom order then place bottom-up into Hinterland bottom-up,then Provinces bottom-up. Fill remaining slots facedown from site deck; flip top site in regions with no faceup site.', 'Law 8.3.5','Map compaction and reverse ruin placement'),
('How are six Archive cards selected for world deck in Chronicle, including suit ties and no suited advisers?', 'Winner most common adviser suit,choose tied suit or any if no suited advisers;three random cards of it,two next clockwise,one next. Clockwise Discord→Arcane→Order→Hearth→Beast→Nomad→Discord.', 'Law 8.4; map favor-bank order','Archive suit selection and clockwise composition'),
('If Archive cannot supply the Chronicle’s required 3/2/1 cards, is a partial allocation added, and how is the Archive healed?', 'Do not add normal allocation. Take all Dispossessed,sort six suit stacks,take six random from largest stack into world deck,shuffle each remaining Dispossessed suit stack into matching Archive stack.', 'Law 8.4','Insufficient Archive alternate procedure'),
('What cards are eligible to become Dispossessed during Chronicle, how many are removed, and what happens to Visions and winner’s advisers?', 'Set aside all five Visions including Conspiracy. Shuffle all region discards with losing players advisers;take six random unseen into Dispossessed. Winner advisers excluded from removal pool;later remaining denizens feed rebuild (site attachments remain saved).', 'Law 8.5,8.8','Dispossessed random removal eligibility'),
('Explain Chronicle relic cleanup order, including Grand Scepter, losing relics, site refill and winner/Reliquary relics.', 'Grand Scepter saved World Box. Losing players relics back relic deck and shuffle. Refill each faceup site to printed R count only if below,place facedown. Shuffle winner remaining held relics with Reliquary relics and put atop relic deck. Site refill precedes winner/Reliquary stacking.', 'Law 8.6','Relic destinations and refill-before-stack timing'),
('How are map cards and boards packed after Chronicle, and does the next group need the same players or status ownership?', 'Stack attached cards on each site;stack sites top Cradle on top,bottom Hinterland bottom,save World Box. Boards saved current Exile/Citizen sides. New people can join;non-Chancellors choose among saved boards in turn order unless group agrees reservations.', 'Law 8.7,1.9; Playbook p31','Persistent map and board state versus people'),
('A matching-suit card is played to a Homeland site after a different-suit card was discarded there this turn. Does reward trigger, what can reward be, and how is a relic reward resolved?', 'Yes provided no card of matching Homeland suit was discarded there this turn. Printed reward: favor or secret from matching bank/shared bank,or two warbands,or take site relic treating as Recover (no ordinary Recover action/site cost). Gain site-play favor then Homeland effect before When Played.', 'Site Reference p2; Law 7.3.3','Homeland suit-specific suppression and direct relic take'),
('How do Coast sites change Travel and interact with Narrow Pass? Is it enough that destination alone is a Coast?', 'From a Coast to another Coast costs one Supply and ignores Narrow Pass;both origin and destination required. Destination-only Coast uses normal costs/restrictions unless another effect applies.', 'Site Reference p2 Coasts','Coast-to-Coast named restriction override'),
('When does Narrow Pass require travel to itself or an added Campaign target, and does ruling Narrow Pass change those conditions?', 'Entering its region from another region must travel to Narrow Pass. Campaign declaring any targets in that region while pawn in different region must also target Narrow Pass unless attacker rules it. The rule exception applies Campaign,not generic entry; named ignore effects can override.', 'Site Reference p2 Narrow Pass','Travel and Campaign gate distinct conditions'),
('What must be paid to travel to Hidden Place or declare Campaign targets there, and which site powers can override this restriction?', 'Flip one board secret facedown;cannot travel/target there without doing so. Shrouded Wood travel ignores Hidden Place;Buried Giant ignores Narrow Pass only,not Hidden Place. Coasts ignore Narrow Pass only.', 'Site Reference p2 Hidden Place,Shrouded Wood,Buried Giant','Hidden Place entry/target payment and named overrides'),
('From Buried Giant, how can you travel without Supply, where does the secret go, and does that automatically ignore Hidden Place?', 'May flip one secret on own board facedown;spend no Supply and ignore Narrow Pass when traveling from there. Secret remains board exhausted,cannot pay again before refresh. Does not name/ignore Hidden Place.', 'Site Reference p2 Buried Giant; Law 7.1.2','Secret exhaustion Travel modifier'),
('How does Marshes change Search, and does it change a remote Search simply because you rule Marshes?', 'Must draw one fewer if pawn there,so ordinary three becomes two,still stop at world Vision/empty source. Rule alone without pawn there does not trigger it.', 'Site Reference p2 Marshes; Law 5.1.2','Pawn-local mandatory Search reduction'),
('When may Great Slum discard a card first, and does this allow discarding there at any unrelated time?', 'When playing or moving a card to this site,may first discard card there,subject locks. It is a timed permission,not unrestricted discard at other times.', 'Site Reference p2 Great Slum; Law 7.2.2','Capacity-clearing timed discard for play/move'),
('Who chooses destination when traveling from enemy-ruled Shrouded Wood, what is its fixed cost, and does forced banishment bypass it?', 'Fixed cost two before other Travel modifiers;ignore Narrow Pass/Hidden Place. If enemy rules it,travel to ruler choice (Chancellor for Empire),even when another player forces travel. Banishment spends no Supply but does not override destination choice.', 'Site Reference p2 Shrouded Wood; Law 5.5.7.III; Errata 5.6','Shrouded Wood forced-travel priority'),
('Do Plains and Mountain modify dice only if the site itself is targeted, and does ruling the site cancel the modifier?', 'Mandatory +one attack die Plains/−one Mountain if any targets at site,including site,even if attacker rules it. Not dependent on site being target itself.', 'Site Reference p2 Plains,Mountain','Target-at-site versus site-target trigger'),
('What additional warband does River grant, and what happens if you Muster there without ruling it?', 'If Muster at River and rule it,gain one more warband,three total ordinary. If do not rule it,ordinary two;eligible empty card,cost still applies and finite bank limit.', 'Site Reference p2 River; Law 5.2,9.3','River rule-dependent Muster outcome'),
('Traveling from Charming Valley in Provinces normally costs how much Supply? What if a spend-no-Supply power is used?', 'Base two plus one increase=three. Spend-no-Supply overrides increase,zero Supply. Fixed-number change applied before increases.', 'Site Reference p2 Charming Valley; Law 7.6.2; Errata 5.6','Origin-based Travel increase versus free override'),
('Who may use Tribunal’s Action, what immediate resources does it let players exchange, and how is a disputed future breach resolved?', 'Its ruler or player whose pawn there may negotiate binding exchange of favor/secrets now,and future actions in combination with any player. Coin flip if unclear whether agreed future promise broken. Does not grant generic immediate exchange of relics/banners.', 'Site Reference p2 Tribunal; Law 7.6.3','Specific binding exchange and future-action permission'),
('How does Bandit Crown affect empty sites, picking up last physical warband, defense and sacrificing bandits?', 'Treat bandits as own warbands:rule empty faceup sites,may pick up last physical at own site,add bandits at targeted sites to defense or relevant attack with powers. Bandits cannot kill/move/sacrifice for skulls,losses,Tyrant/Cursed Cauldron.', 'Law 7.6.5','Virtual warband benefits without expendability'),
('Can a player rule a facedown site or put cards there using a move power? What does a ruined edifice contribute to capacity, suit and action access?', 'No:only faceup sites ruled and facedown sites cannot hold cards. Ruin counts denizen/edifice capacity,has no suit,cannot Muster/Trade,but its power still functions per access/text.', 'Law 2.8–9; Errata 2.8,Rule','Facedown sites and ruined-edifice restrictions'),
('Must every draw from the world deck follow the entire Search draw-stop procedure, or does the corrected Draw glossary differ? What always happens when a Vision is drawn from world deck?', 'Corrected Draw simply takes top cards from prompted source;does not automatically import all Search rules into other powers. Always advance Visions Drawn for world-deck Vision,including Oracle. Search itself must stop at world Vision.', 'Errata Draw; Law 2.7.1,5.1.2','Generic Draw versus Search overspecification correction'),
('Can you take several major/minor actions in any order, stop without spending all Supply, or begin another action before current one finishes?', 'Any number/order/repeats including none while costs payable;may stop and preserve unspent Supply through Rest;must finish current action before next. No interrupting Campaign with another normal minor action.', 'Law 4.2–3','Action sequencing and voluntary rest'),
('If you seize a banner by Conspiracy or a binding transfer rather than Campaign, does it lose resources? How does Recover differ?', 'Any taking except Recover is seizure;burn two banner favor/secrets down to minimum one,People’s Favor Mob. Recover instead replaces resources with paid outbid,distributes old as described,and People’s Favor normal. No burn-two seizure on Recover.', 'Law 2.5.3,Glossary Seize,5.4','Seizure scope beyond Campaign'),
('Can a Citizen’s defensive battle plan prohibit other Allies’ battle plans, and who decides contested order or competing use of a shared plan?', 'Power references you/defender cover whole defending side,so cannot-use-other-plans limits all Allies. Your site/board remain individual. Declared defender resolves order/priority and competing shared use;one specific plan once total,user pays.', 'Errata 5.5; Law 5.5.3','Sidewide prohibitions and defender arbitration'),
('When a new Citizen’s conversion needs more purple warbands than available, who decides what is removed, and what is converted when that Citizen later becomes Exile?', 'New Citizen chooses which existing board/map warbands to replace purple and which to remove for shortage. Later exile converts only board warbands to own color;map garrisons stay purple. Gain/take source shortage maximum possible.', 'Law 6.6.2,6.7–8,9.3','Conversion shortfall choices versus later exile scope'),
('If the People’s Favor is normal with five favor and its holder adds one at Wake, how many choices happen this Wake? What if it was already Mob?', 'Normal begins with one choice;add sixth then final check flips Mob,no retroactive second choice. Already Mob makes two choices,each obeying last-favor restriction;does not revert just by falling below six.', 'Law 4.1.1','Mob threshold timing and non-reversion'),
('Can an Exile holding an unrevealed true Vision win at Wake, or reveal it at Wake to win immediately? What if fewer than three world Visions have been drawn?', 'No:must already have revealed and complete at victory check;normal reveal minor action in Act,not Wake. Fewer than three world Visions blocks Visionary even if goal assets met;may reveal earlier for future.', 'Law 3.2,4.1.2,6.1','Vision revelation deadline and global gate'),
('Can an Exile whose title has not yet flipped to Usurper win as Oathkeeper at end of round eight? If not, who can win instead?', 'Oathkeeper alone not Usurper win;priority Empire-Oathkeeper absent if Exile holds,then existing Usurper,then qualifying Visionary,then Empire fallback with possible Successor. Exile can still win qualifying revealed Vision.', 'Law 3.4','Eighth-round Exile-Oathkeeper-only fallback'),
('At Chronicle, if Exile wins through both Usurper and Vision, must next Oath match Vision? Who may receive Chronicle Citizenship and how are accepting site garrisons replaced?', 'Multiple-method win chooses any Oath except current,not forced Vision match. Flip all Citizen boards Exile;winner may offer other Exiles except just-flipped former Citizens,not self. Accepting Exile sites replace all garrisons with one winner-color warband per ruled site;no normal Reliquary gift.', 'Law 8.1–2; Errata 8.2','Combined-win Oath and Chronicle citizenship garrison collapse'),
('When playing through People’s Favor, must discarded and receiving sites be identical, can the discard come from another region, and can a locked card be discarded?', 'Sites may differ but both must be in pawn region;cannot use power to discard elsewhere. Locked faceup card cannot be discarded. Receiving site capacity still applies;gain played-card suit favor as normal.', 'Law 5.1.4.I,7.2.2','Regional redirection and lock/capacity interaction'),
('If a victorious attacker targeted pawn/favor and a banner, must they banish, must they burn favor, and must they take the banner? What is the rounding of board favor burn?', 'Banish optional;board favor burn independently optional,half rounded down. Taking all targeted relics/banners mandatory. Seized banner burns two its resources min one separately from optional board-favor burn.', 'Law 5.5.7','Optional target consequences versus mandatory booty'),
('What do skulls do if you chose fewer attack dice than board warbands, and can you sacrifice more than required to win to reduce your upkeep?', 'Each skull kills own force warband immediately,not one per rolled die necessarily nor defender. Choice of fewer dice does not shrink force to those dice for casualties. Sacrifice exactly necessary to win if choose,never surplus to adjust upkeep.', 'Law 5.5.2,5.5.5–6,9.5','Dice choice does not redefine force or permit extra sacrifice'),
('What does the Exile/Chancellor Supply refresh depend on exactly, and how much Supply do their personal-bank brackets give before saving?', 'Unused personal-bank warbands,not board/map. Chancellor 18+:6,11–17:5,4–10:4,0–3:3. Exile9+:6,4–8:5,0–3:4. Add saved remaining Supply capped at full seven. Citizen instead exact Chancellor marker.', 'Law 4.3.3–4; player boards Playbook p3','Numeric Supply brackets and personal-bank domain')
]
q=json.loads((P/'seed-v1/questions.json').read_text());k=json.loads((P/'seed-v1/answer-key.json').read_text());q['benchmark_version']='expanded-v1';k['benchmark_version']='expanded-v1'
accepted=[]
for n,(question,answer,refs,novelty) in enumerate(rows,21):
 id=f'Q{n:03}';q['questions'].append({'id':id,'question':question});k['answers'].append({'id':id,'expected_answer':answer,'material_facts':answer.split('; '),'source_references':refs});accepted.append({'id':id,'source_references':refs,'novelty':novelty,'accepted':True})
d=P/'expanded-v1';d.mkdir(exist_ok=True)
for name,data in [('questions.json',q),('answer-key.json',k)]: (d/name).write_text(json.dumps(data,indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)+'\n')
(d/'question-bank.md').write_text('# Oath expanded bank v1\n\n'+ '\n\n'.join(f"## {a['id']}\n\n{b['question']}\n\n**Answer:** {a['expected_answer']}\n\n**Source:** {a['source_references']}" for a,b in zip(k['answers'],q['questions']))+'\n')
(d/'input-manifest.json').write_text(json.dumps({f:hashlib.sha256((d/f).read_bytes()).hexdigest() for f in ['questions.json','answer-key.json']},indent=2)+'\n')
(P/'coverage-additions.json').write_text(json.dumps(accepted,indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)+'\n');print('Count',len(q['questions']))
